## Location
- /Volumes/Attic/Desktop/Projects/crates/schc/src/fragment/ack_always.rs lines 356-368

## Problem
The receiver appends each fragment payload sequentially at self.offset:

```rust
// Calculate buffer position
let tile_offset = self.offset;
let end = tile_offset + frag.payload.len();
// ...
self.buffer[tile_offset..end].copy_from_slice(frag.payload);
self.offset = end;
```

This assumes fragments arrive in order (FCN descending within window). If fragments arrive out of order (e.g., FCN 5 arrives before FCN 6), the reassembled data will be corrupted.

## What Goes Wrong
Given fragments for FCN 6, 5, 4:
- If they arrive 6, 5, 4: buffer contains [tile6][tile5][tile4] - correct
- If they arrive 5, 6, 4: buffer contains [tile5][tile6][tile4] - tiles at wrong offsets

Compare to AckOnErrorReceiver which calculates the correct buffer position from window and FCN.

## Suggested Fix
Calculate buffer position from fragment position:
```rust
let position_in_window = WINDOW_SIZE - 1 - frag.fcn as usize;
let global_position = window as usize * WINDOW_SIZE + position_in_window;
let tile_offset = global_position * TILE;
```
